cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Nyx: a flexible framework for sleep scoring across species, lifespan and modalities"
message: "If you use this software, please cite the preprint below."
type: software
license: LGPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-04"

# Add this once the repository exists, so the "Cite this repository" button and
# any Zenodo archive point at the right place:
# repository-code: "https://github.com/<org>/nyx"

abstract: >-
  Nyx scores sleep from EEG and EMG without training data or manually scored
  examples. It separates wake from sleep using EMG power, then splits sleep into
  stages by clustering a principal component analysis of the EEG spectrogram.
  Scoring is expressed as an ordered sequence of clustering steps, so rodent
  three-stage scoring and human five-stage scoring run the same code and differ
  only in configuration.

keywords:
  - sleep scoring
  - polysomnography
  - electroencephalography
  - electromyography
  - hypnogram
  - unsupervised clustering
  - electrophysiology

